 damaged  more than a thousand people have been  evacuated from a five kilometer radius  and at this stage it looks like it's  still not under control  and tony it was a it was a plastics  manufacturing  uh building wasn't it where this began  do we know any more about what might  have caused the initial explosion there  at this stage we don't it was producing  foam for  for packaging but there's a lot of  industry in that area and we've seen  reports in the past couple of years of  people using  unlicensed or unregulated chemicals  again at this stage  very hard to know exactly what's going  on but  uh initial estimates are saying that  it's caused 21 million dollars worth of  damage  already to the ming d manufacturing  plant where it was  and i think there's growing concern that  as it burns out of control  it is it's going to be an obstruction to  the international airport so one of them  which is right next door at certain  points as well it's only three  kilometers away  and that black plume of smoke is uh  getting closer and closer to the airport  the authorities say that air travel has  not yet been disrupted  i think if there continues to be this  large amount of toxic smoke  and the threat of further explosions  that may soon be revised  all right for now uh thank you for that  update tony cheng in bangkok
 

